        "answer": {
          "short": "$h=-2$, $k=1$.",
          "worked": "The vertex in vertex form is $(h,k)$. Comparing with $(-2,1)$ gives $h=-2$ and $k=1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "The parabola also passes through the point $(1,2)$. Find the value of the last pronumeral and hence, find the equation of the parabola.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=\\frac19$; $y=\\frac19(x+2)^2+1$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=a(x+2)^2+1\\\\2&=a(1+2)^2+1\\\\2&=9a+1\\\\a&=\\frac19\\\\y&=\\frac19(x+2)^2+1.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
